+    ``coefficient`` is deliberately expressed as a ratio of a boundary
+    integral and a configurational integral.  If Z is the configurational
+    partition integral, phi is
+
+        (1 - exp(-2 L)) / (2 N) * d(log Z)/dL,
+
+    where L = log(R/a).  That form avoids numerical differentiation of a
+    free energy.
+    """
